Hello,

I've made a testing RxODE shiny app which runs fine on my own computer. It just won't run on shinyapps.io <http://shinyapps.io> online though and I keep seeing this error message:
ERROR: Error sourcing /srv/connect/apps/myapp/app.R

I'm suspecting it's because the package needs to send the code to a temporary folder on the local computer with a compiler - it requires Rtools on the local computer to run - and dynamically load that back to R. In fact, the app won't run properly if the temporary folder is not specified. Is there a way we can run this kind of app on shinyapps.io <http://shinyapps.io>?

Thanks so you for your help.

